    "description": "Pin the cases at aa720c0 and write the new low-effort baseline\n\nThis PR moves the cases pin to jerridan/pr-review-cases@aa720c0 and writes a new baseline for it. That commit adds three goldens (jerridan/pr-review-cases#1). A change of the case set needs a new baseline.\n\n## The baseline run\n\nI ran the eval locally on this branch, with reviewer effort low, 3 repeats:\n\n```\npr-review eval --cases eval/cases --repeat 3 --baseline eval/baseline.json --write-baseline\n```\n\n| Case | Recall per repeat | Precision | Cost per repeat |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| fixture-off-by-one | 0.600, 0.400, 0.400 | 1.000 | $1.14–$2.80 |\n| pr-4-consumer-workflow | 0, 0, 0 | — | $2.83–$4.31 |\n| pr-5-tests-reviewer-checks | 0, 0, 0 | — | $0.58–$0.85 |\n| pr-6-review-body-summary | 0, 0, 0 | — | $1.72–$3.33 |\n\nAggregate: recall mean 0.117 (min 0.100), precision 1.000, cost per case $2.23.\n\nI checked each of the 12 records. Each verdict is complete, and no record holds an error. An earlier run hit the session limit of the Claude login. Its incomplete repeats counted as valid runs, so I discarded it. #15 fixes that defect in the eval.\n\n## The margins\n\n- **Recall: 0.05** (was 0.10). The spread is 0.017. Doubled and rounded up, it gives 0.05. Step 5 of the margin rules also limits the margin to 0.05, because 0.10 is less than 0.05 below the baseline value of 0.117.\n- **Precision: 0.35** (no change). This run had no spread. The rules say to use the larger spread of the recent baseline runs, so the margin stays.\n\nThe README paragraph on the starter set now gives the new numbers.\n\n## Next\n\nAfter the merge, PR #13 (reviewer effort medium) rebases on main, so its eval runs against this baseline.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UKXoH72K6RLXNCGUFmHPfP\n",
